CEILING = trade the early touch toward the eventual close, when they differ by >=1c, net of 0.07*p*(1-p).
It is look-ahead; a real model captures some fraction of it, and only if a real-time reference moves first.
The controls (buy YES always / buy NO always at the same early touch) show what a one-sided bias alone earns.
